raw_content:
Now the big one: ArtifactServiceImpl. Rewrite fully in ~2 segments (each ≤ ~200 lines). Let me draft the whole file.

Key parts:
- registerArtifact: validate (incl. capabilities: ≤3, distinct, non-blank, ≤64 after trim — trim each), structured hash, executeIdempotent.
- withdrawArtifact: structured hash.
- addExclusion / removeExclusion: validate request (a≠b after trim → 400), structured hash with operator, executeIdempotent.
- listExclusions.
- createLock: structured hash, doLock.
- listLocks / getLock with frozen capabilities + exclusions.
- doRegister, doWithdraw, doAddExclusion, doRemoveExclusion, doLock.
- executeIdempotent, replayIfPresent (unchanged).
- validation helpers, hash builders, json helpers, sha256.

Structured hash builders:

```java
private String registerHash(RegisterArtifactRequest request) {
    ObjectNode identity = objectMapper.createObjectNode();
    identity.put("operation", OP_REGISTER);
    identity.put("resource", request.name().trim());
    identity.put("version", request.version());
    ArrayNode dependencies = identity.putArray("dependencies");
    request.dependencies().stream()
            .sorted(Comparator.comparing(d -> d.name().trim()))
            .forEach(dep -> {
                ObjectNode node = dependencies.addObject();
                node.put("name", dep.name().trim());
                node.put("minimumVersion", dep.minimumVersion());
                node.put("maximumVersion", dep.maximumVersion());
            });
    ArrayNode capabilities = identity.putArray("capabilities");
    normalizedCapabilities(request).forEach(capabilities::add);
    return sha256(identity.toString());
}
```

Wait — normalizedCapabilities trims and sorts; but validation happens before hash. Order: validate first, then hash. In registerArtifact: validateRegisterRequest(request) then compute hash.

normalizedCapabilities: trim each, sort, dedupe? Duplicates → 400 in validation. So normalized = sorted trimmed list.

doLock needs capabilities per chosen artifact: after resolve, look up snapshot:

```java
Map<String, ArtifactVersion> chosenArtifacts = new HashMap<>();
solution.forEach((n, v) -> {
    ArtifactVersion av = snapshot.artifacts().get(n).stream()
            .filter(a -> a.version() == v).findFirst()
            .orElseThrow(...);
    chosenArtifacts.put(n, av);
});
```

Then insert lock entries + capabilities sorted, and exclusions from snapshot.exclusions().

Response entries: LockEntryResponse(name, version, capabilities sorted). Exclusions: List<CapabilityPairView>.

toLockResponse(row, entries, capsMap, exclusions).

doAddExclusion:

```java
private ExclusionRuleResponse doAddExclusion(ExclusionRuleRequest request) {
    long currentVersion = repositoryDao.lockRepositoryState(); // already locked at entry; but doLock re-locks — FOR UPDATE again is fine (same tx). Actually executeIdempotent already locks. doLock calls lockRepositoryState again to read version. I'll follow same pattern: call lockRepositoryState() to get current version.
    if (currentVersion != request.expectedRepositoryVersion()) throw conflict 409;
    CapabilityPair pair = CapabilityPair.of(a, b);
    if (repositoryDao.exclusionExists(pair)) throw conflict 409 "互斥规则已存在";
    if (repositoryDao.countExclusions() >= MAX_EXCLUSIONS) throw unprocessable 422;
    Instant now = ...;
    repositoryDao.insertExclusion(pair, now);
    long newVersion = repositoryDao.incrementRepositoryVersion();
    return new ExclusionRuleResponse(pair.first(), pair.second(), newVersion, now);
}
```

doRemoveExclusion: check version; if !exists → 404; delete; increment; return response.

Validation of exclusion request in service (bean validation handles blank at HTTP layer, but service-level calls need checks): trim, non-blank, ≤64, a≠b → 400 "能力相同不互斥".

Normalization helper:

```java
private static CapabilityPair normalizedPair(ExclusionRuleRequest request) {
    String a = request.capabilityA() == null ? null : request.capabilityA().trim();
    String b = ...;
    if (a == null || a.isEmpty() || b == null || b.isEmpty()) throw badRequest("能力名不能为空");
    if (a.length() > 64 || b.length() > 64) throw badRequest("能力名长度不能超过 64");
    if (a.equals(b)) throw badRequest("能力相同不构成互斥: " + a);
    return CapabilityPair.of(a, b);
}
```

Exclusion hash:

```java
private String exclusionHash(String operation, String operator, CapabilityPair pair, long expectedVersion) {
    ObjectNode identity = objectMapper.createObjectNode();
    identity.put("operation", operation);
    identity.put("operator", operator == null ? "" : operator);
    identity.put("capabilityA", pair.first());
    identity.put("capabilityB", pair.second());
    identity.put("expectedRepositoryVersion", expectedVersion);
    return sha256(identity.toString());
}
```

Withdraw hash:

```java
ObjectNode: operation, resource=name, version
```

Lock hash: operation, resource=rootName, rootVersion, expectedRepositoryVersion.

Note: previous hashes were sha256 of pipe-joined strings; changing hash format is fine (no persisted data to migrate; in-mem H2).

Register validation additions:

```java
List<String> capabilities = request.capabilities();
if (capabilities.size() > 3) throw badRequest("每个制品版本最多声明 3 个能力");
Set<String> capNames = new HashSet<>();
for (String cap : capabilities) {
    if (cap == null || cap.isBlank()) throw badRequest("能力名不能为空");
    String trimmed = cap.trim();
    if (trimmed.length() > 64) throw badRequest("能力名长度不能超过 64: " + trimmed);
    if (!capNames.add(trimmed)) throw badRequest("能力名重复: " + trimmed);
}
```

doRegister: insert capabilities (trimmed, sorted for determinism), response capabilities sorted.

doWithdraw: response capabilities from artifact.capabilities() sorted.

toDependencyViews unchanged.

